      "message": "I don\u0027t understand why this is needed.  The resync function does the following:\n* clear SETTLED_EVENT\n* Set CCI_EVENT in the cci_flags\n* wait for SETTLED_EVENT\n\nThe run state of all parent states (unattached, type-c only, sink, source) all check CCI_EVENT and queue up a GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS.  Once that command completes, the run_*_policies() function calls send_pending_public_commands() which posts SETTLED_EVENT.\n\nAre you certain the PDC thread was idle when the you saw settled event timeout?\n\nMy concern is that unconditionally posting SETTLED_EVENT on a timer may cause callers to resync to exit early.",
